24m4|n|A shade for the face, projecting from the bonnet.	V:1ukf,15,1~1ukf,15,1	N:1d5e,25,1;1v07,8,1~1d5e,25,1;1v07,8,1
24m4|v|To make ugly.	o:1v07,18,2~1v07,18,2
24m4|a|Offensive to the sight; contrary to beauty; being of disagreeable or loathsome aspect; unsightly; repulsive; deformed. ; Ill-natured; crossgrained; quarrelsome; as, an ugly temper; to feel ugly. ; Unpleasant; disagreeable; likely to cause trouble or loss; as, an ugly rumor; an ugly customer.	j:1d5e,35,2;1ukf,15,1;1d57,12,1;djq,12,1;1v07,8,1~1d5e,35,2;1v07,8,1;1ukf,15,1;1d57,12,1;djq,12,1
